##
##    PrePoMax --> code_aster from "pmx2aster.py" V0.1.5 | [ 11-Dec-2025 ] 
##    Made by Sound Spinning | soundspinning@hotmail.com
##    Meant to be run from a terminal with `run_aster *.export` instead of with `as_run`
##

 #  "rig_it1_assy_brackets_1.inp" model HEADING:
 # Hash: xnrlIrvq, Date: 01/21/2026, Unit system: MM_TON_S_C
 # ITER1 - Brackets assembly:
 # Test model with unit loads to compare rigid vs soft couplings.
 # These affect loads, constraints & joints.
 # ----------------------------------------

### RAM in MB - Since V16.7 the solver grabs 90% of this input
P memory_limit 64000
P ncpus 1
### max solve time in seconds ==> 4e5s = 4.63days 
P time_limit 400000.0

## Input deck
F comm rig_it1_assy_brackets_1.comm D  1

## Input mesh - ASTER format
F mesh rig_it1_assy_brackets_1.msh D  21

## Output message file
F mesg rig_it1_assy_brackets_1.msg R  6

## Output text results file
F data rig_it1_assy_brackets_1.dat R  8

## MED results file#1
F rmed rig_it1_assy_brackets_1.rmed R  80
## MED results file#2
F rmed rig_it1_assy_brackets_1_points_springs.rmed R  81

## Output FOLDER for global restart files, also useful for Sub-modelling
## When reading the `base` in a restart run, change RC --> DC
## R base rig_it1_assy_brackets_1 RC 0

## Output local temp FOLDER (if needed) for solver temp (.med) files
## R repe TMP R  0
